abstract: >-
  WarpAX uses JAX automatic differentiation to compute exact curvature tensors
  from analytic warp drive metrics and decides the null, weak, strong and
  dominant energy conditions over every timelike observer at once, from the
  positive semidefiniteness of a single 4x4 linear matrix inequality, with a
  continuous BFGS search over the observer manifold as the independent
  cross-check.  Reported verdicts carry exact rational certificates, and
  interval branch-and-bound supplies verified continuum enclosures of the
  worst-case violation.  The toolkit includes source-consistency modules for Einstein
  constraint residuals, anisotropic TOV equilibrium, ADM mass, Israel junction
  conditions, and invariant transport diagnostics, as well as source-first shell
  construction (S-shell Class I, T-shell Class II) with Bernstein-parameterized
  profiles and constraint-derived metric potentials.
